cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "plant-chemistry-skills: agent skills linking plant biodiversity to chemistry"
message: "If you use these skills, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bissol
    given-names: Gary Paul
    affiliation: Byss Group SASU, Fort-de-France, Martinique
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Oshinsu/plant-chemistry-skills"
keywords:
  - agent skills
  - natural products
  - metabolomics
  - taxonomy
  - biodiversity
  - research bias
abstract: >-
  Six agent skills that connect plant biodiversity data to natural-product
  chemistry: WCVP name resolution with full synonym expansion, LOTUS chemistry
  lookup with a blocking golden-record guardrail, GBIF collection effort as a
  control covariate, public mass-spectrometry repository lookup via Pan-ReDU,
  natural-product database licensing, and six methodological controls for
  chemical coverage analysis. The controls encode five false results that were
  produced and caught during a real analysis of Lesser Antilles flora: tests
  without statistical power, baselines contaminated by crop species,
  phylogenetic non-independence inflating p-values by a factor of 1.87 per
  degree of freedom, occurrence-derived range proxies confounded with
  collection effort, and hand-made cultivation filters missing most of what
  they were meant to remove.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The LOTUS initiative for open knowledge management in natural products
